ld_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\n\n- Reproducible in: 4.4.dev7 \n- Not reproducible in: 4.3.stable\n\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.3.stable - Windows 10.0.19045 - GLES3 (Compatibility) - AMD Radeon RX 6650 XT (Advanced Micro Devices, Inc.; 32.0.12033.1030) - AMD Ryzen 5 5600G with Radeon Graphics (12 Threads)\n\n### Issue description\n\nCTRL + Clicking on a variable that's referenced from a global-autoload file, now takes you to the auto-generated help for that file, rather than taking to the referenced variable. As-though the global-autoload is now regarded as a class.\n\nIn 4.3.stable, you'd be taken straight to that variable;\n\n\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nVideo: https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/15287001-780d-4c26-82f7-bd797eacb6ee\n\n---\n\n```gd\n# ./globals/core.gd\nextends Node;\n\nvar is_paused:bool;\n```\n\n```gd\n# ./main.gd\nextends Node;\n\nfunc _ready() -> void:\n\tCore.is_paused = true;\n```\n\nAdd the `./globals/core.gd` file as a Global Autoload, then CTRL + Click on the `is_paused` variable in `./main.gd`.\n\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\nMRP: [44dev7.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/18216768/44dev7.zip)\n","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/